title One denied command and its approved retry

model  "Model"
tool   "bash tool"
runner "Sandbox runner"
appr   "Approval"
usr    "/usr/local"
asks   "Approvals asked" counter 0

c1, c2 at model

# The session is in workspace-write, so writes outside the project fail.
pause "The model wants to run npm install -g typescript, which writes to /usr/local."

# The first try runs confined, and the kernel refuses the write.
c1 -> tool : running "The standing mode is workspace-write."
c1 -> runner : running "Writes are allowed only under the project and temp folders."
c1 : failed "Writing /usr/local/lib is outside the write roots."
c1 -> model : failed "The result carries the denial line and the hint to retry once."

# The retry names a wider mode and says why.
c2 -> tool : waiting "sandbox_permissions is danger-full-access, with a one-sentence justification."
c2 -> appr : waiting "The person sees the command, the mode and the reason."
asks +1

# A yes covers this one call only.
c2 -> usr : done "allowed-once: this call alone runs without the runner."
pause "The next command runs in workspace-write again."
